  "justification": "Core genome-wide quantities (G+C content, tRNA count, rRNA operon count, and CDS co-orientation with replication) reproduce closely on NC_000913.3, consistent with expected minor drift from curation and resequencing. Genome size and protein-coding gene count differ modestly (≈0.05% longer; +30 CDSs), plausibly attributable to sequence error correction and annotation refinement rather than a failure of the original report. Coding density and mean CDS length are directionally consistent but show larger differences (≈1.7 percentage points and ≈1.3% shorter, respectively), suggesting annotation updates materially affect these derived metrics. Several listed measurements (start-codon usage and base composition breakdown) were not explicitly tabulated as claims in the 1997 paper, limiting claim-level coverage."
